<title>USA: U.S. stockpile accepts antimony offers.</title>
<headline>U.S. stockpile accepts antimony offers.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Defense National Stockpile Center announced it sold 3,481,467 pounds (1,579 tonnes) of antimony for an approximate current market value of $3 million.</p>
<p>The awards were made to Amalgamated Metal, London; Aaron Ferer &amp; Sons Co, Nebraska; and Nonfemet Resource Ltd of New Jersey.</p>
<p>The next opening of offers for antimony, beryl ore and cadmium will be January 14, 1997 at 1400 EST.</p>
<p>-- New York Commodities 212-859-1646</p>
</text>
